- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — entity; `registrationDate` field at line 53-54, getter/setter 97-103.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct mapping, computes `membershipNumber` on output.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — schema; `registrationDate` at lines 2040-2045, `membershipNumber` at 2096-2101.

## 2. Where registrationDate is set/defaulted

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`, lines 11-16:

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(java.time.LocalDate.now());
    }
    built.set(owner);
}
```

The value is taken from the request if supplied, otherwise defaulted to `LocalDate.now()` (raw server date). Note: it defaults to the plain calendar date — there is NO business-day/weekend rolling in production code (see gap note below). The OpenAPI doc confirms this contract at `openapi.yml:2042` ("Defaults to the current server date when omitted.").

## 3. Where the membership number is generated (year segment)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/MembershipNumber.java`, lines 14-16:

```java
public static String of(String customerCode, LocalDate registrationDate) {
    return String.format("%s-M%02d", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
}
```

Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where the year segment `YY` is `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (last two digits). It is invoked from the output mapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`, lines 25-26 (computed at response time, not persisted). The `customerCode` half is produced by `AssignCustomerCode.java` as `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`.

## 4. Where the daily create-limit logic lives

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RequireDailyCapacity.java`, full file:

```java
static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;

public void service(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyLimitException {
    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
    long count = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
        .count();
    if (count >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
        throw new DailyLimitException(count);
    }
}
```

Limit is 100 owners whose `registrationDate` equals today. On breach it throws `DailyLimitException`. Supporting escalation classes:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyLimitException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyLimitExceptionHandler.java` — responds HTTP 429 (TOO_MANY_REQUESTS)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyLimitException.yml` — wires the handler

## 5. Existing tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`, lines 14-19 — the only active assertion for this area:

```java
@Test
void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
    DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
    assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
}
```

The class javadoc (lines 9-11) states the intended rule: "the default registration date must fall on a business day (a weekend rolls forward to Monday)."

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — test-side helpers/fixtures:
- `createMany(int n)` lines 181-187 — creates n owners dated today, "to drive the per-day create-limit / bulk-signup rules."
- `HOLIDAYS` set, lines 239-242 (pinned 2026 public holidays).
- `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` lines 267-274 — rolls a date forward over Saturdays, Sundays, and `HOLIDAYS` to the next business day.
- Comment at line 182 references the "per-day create-limit / bulk-signup rules."

## Business-day / weekend / holiday utility code

There is NO business-day/weekend/holiday utility in production/main code — `grep` for `business.?day|weekend|holiday|DayOfWeek` matched only the two test files. The only implementation of business-day rolling lives in the test base (`AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay` + `HOLIDAYS`, lines 239-274).

Notable gap: `BuildOwner` defaults `registrationDate` to a raw `LocalDate.now()` with no weekend/holiday adjustment, yet `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` (and the documented rule) expects the default to never be a Saturday/Sunday. If the server runs on a weekend the production default would violate the test's asserted invariant, so the business-day-roll logic appears to be specified/tested but not yet implemented in the create flow.

